-- THE JS MODEL AS A LIBRARY OF THE ENGINE: what `@js` names (docs/cli.md, *Model libraries*).
-- The library has a version of its own and says which engine it needs; an older engine refuses it and says both.
library(js, "1.0.0").
needs_engine(js, "1.7.0").
-- the files of the model, in the order they load, from this directory
files(js, "js.files").
-- what turns a directory of JS/TS into the facts the model reads: its command and the form of its output
scanner(js, "rofl scan", text).
